From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:15:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-pci-gli: optionally runtime suspend an
 idle GL9755

The GL9755 has no runtime PM, so an SD reader without a card stays in
D0 for as long as the system runs. The GL9763E already runtime
suspends, but it serves eMMC, which cannot be removed.

A GL9755 slot can: runtime suspend masks every interrupt but the SDIO
card interrupt, including card detect, and the slot has no card detect
GPIO. So when runtime PM is allowed, ask the core to poll for a card
(MMC_CAP_NEEDS_POLL); each poll resumes the host, and autosuspend puts
it back after 50 ms.

The vendor configuration written at probe, card detect and write
protect inversion included, is not known to survive D3hot, so it is
applied again on runtime resume before the host is used.

Keep it off by default behind gl9755_runtime_pm, read when the device
is bound: with it off nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
index b55618566d..0a3eb26daf 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-pci-gli.c
@@ -20,6 +20,11 @@
 #include "cqhci.h"
 #include "sdhci-uhs2.h"
 
+static bool gl9755_runtime_pm;
+module_param(gl9755_runtime_pm, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(gl9755_runtime_pm,
+		 "Runtime suspend an idle GL9755, polling for a card once a second; read when the device is bound (default: off)");
+
 /*  Genesys Logic extra registers */
 #define SDHCI_GLI_9750_WT         0x800
 #define   SDHCI_GLI_9750_WT_EN      BIT(0)
@@ -1591,6 +1596,15 @@ static int gli_probe_slot_gl9755(struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot)
 	sdhci_enable_v4_mode(host);
 	gl9755_vendor_init(host);
 
+	/*
+	 * Runtime suspend masks the card detect interrupt, and the slot has
+	 * no card detect GPIO, so a card is then found by polling.
+	 */
+	if (gl9755_runtime_pm) {
+		host->mmc->caps |= MMC_CAP_NEEDS_POLL;
+		slot->chip->allow_runtime_pm = true;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1867,6 +1881,31 @@ static void gl9763e_hw_setting(struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot)
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
+static int gl9755_runtime_suspend(struct sdhci_pci_chip *chip)
+{
+	struct sdhci_host *host = chip->slots[0]->host;
+
+	sdhci_runtime_suspend_host(host);
+	if (chip->rpm_retune && host->tuning_mode != SDHCI_TUNING_MODE_3)
+		mmc_retune_needed(host->mmc);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int gl9755_runtime_resume(struct sdhci_pci_chip *chip)
+{
+	struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot = chip->slots[0];
+
+	/*
+	 * The vendor configuration, card detect inversion included, is not
+	 * known to survive D3hot: apply it again before using the host.
+	 */
+	gl9755_hw_setting(slot);
+	sdhci_runtime_resume_host(slot->host, 0);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int gl9763e_runtime_suspend(struct sdhci_pci_chip *chip)
 {
 	struct sdhci_pci_slot *slot = chip->slots[0];
@@ -2054,6 +2093,11 @@ const struct sdhci_pci_fixes sdhci_gl9755 = {
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
 	.resume         = sdhci_pci_gli_resume,
 #endif
+#ifdef CONFIG_PM
+	/* Used only when gl9755_runtime_pm allows runtime PM at probe */
+	.runtime_suspend = gl9755_runtime_suspend,
+	.runtime_resume  = gl9755_runtime_resume,
+#endif
 };
 
 static const struct sdhci_ops sdhci_gl9750_ops = {
